WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.620
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:12.300
This is GPT-4, OpenAI’s new language model AI&nbsp;
that we just talked about, and today I would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.880
love to show you that it has barely been out,&nbsp;
and it is already taking the world by storm.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:24.720
Here are 5 incredible ways it already is&nbsp;
in use in the real world, in real products,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:31.560
some of which you can probably try right now,&nbsp;
or at the very least, soon. One. In the language&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:38.700
learning app Duolingo, they now supercharged the&nbsp;
process of learning a new language with GPT-4.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:45.840
We can have scripted conversations, for instance,&nbsp;
we can order coffee in French. That is very cool,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:54.180
but that’s not the interesting part. Yet. Now,&nbsp;
look! GPT-4 will look at our conversation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:01:00.000
give us tips on how to make our French feel&nbsp;
a little more natural. And don’t forget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.820
this can be a two-way conversation, so&nbsp;
if we don’t quite understand what it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.740
trying to teach us, we can also ask&nbsp;
for additional examples. Loving it.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:17.820
Two, Stripe, a payment processor company&nbsp;
puts GPT-4’s amazing information organizing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:24.300
capabilities to use by letting the users&nbsp;
ask them a question in natural text. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:29.100
normally, if we have a question like&nbsp;
this, we would have to look through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:34.020
entire documentation and hope there is&nbsp;
something about it. But, from today on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:42.000
not anymore. Instead, we can now ask GPT-4 to&nbsp;
look through their entire documentation and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.000
summarize the solution for us. This is going&nbsp;
to save a lot of time for a lot of people.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.920
Three, my favorite, Khan Academy is also testing&nbsp;
a GPT-4 powered solution. If you are a student,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.940
and have a question about, for instance,&nbsp;
mathematics, and the best part is, it will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:08.520
behave like a real tutor and will not just give&nbsp;
you the solution, but it can also try to steer you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:15.360
towards that solution and give you hints so you&nbsp;
can find it out yourself. This is going to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:22.560
millions and millions of children study all around&nbsp;
the world. And, it can also help with perhaps the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:29.400
most dreaded question a computer science student&nbsp;
can ask. And of course, that is “Here is my piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:37.020
of code, but it’s not working. What’s wrong with&nbsp;
it?”. And it can help us with that too. That is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:43.980
absolutely amazing. What a time to be alive! It&nbsp;
can also help teachers create a curriculum too.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:49.920
Four, while we are talking about&nbsp;
helping us write and fix computer code,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:56.040
it can look at our whole codebase, and&nbsp;
whenever some issue arises it can not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.420
only tell us what is going on, but,&nbsp;
it will actually write that missing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:06.660
subtraction function and fix the return&nbsp;
variable as well in one go. So cool!

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:15.360
And five, it can also be connected to your car,&nbsp;
and we can ask it about our average speed and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:22.860
current status of our battery. But that would not&nbsp;
be as useful. Can it do something that requires a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:29.100
little more intelligence? Of course it can!&nbsp;
Look! It can even create a plot that shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:36.240
our speed and our battery drain for each of our&nbsp;
previous driving sessions. And that’s just the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:42.660
first few experiments of trying to make this&nbsp;
incredible new AI work. And it already helps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:49.200
us learn new languages, organize our knowledge,&nbsp;
it can become an excellent tutor when studying,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:56.460
helps us fixing computer code, and also&nbsp;
makes our car more useful. How cool is that!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:04.680
And don’t forget, GPT-4 is multimodal, so we&nbsp;
can not only give it text as an input, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:11.820
images too. We can ask it to explain memes, tell&nbsp;
us what would happen in hypothetical scenarios.

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:18.360
And just imagine what this will be able to&nbsp;
do just two more papers down the line. Maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:26.040
a personal assistant who reads news and papers&nbsp;
for us, it knows our interests and summarizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:32.940
them just in the way we like it, check its sources&nbsp;
and points out potential flaws in the reasoning.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:40.860
I would love that. But you know what? Perhaps&nbsp;
GPT-4 can already do that, we just need to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:47.580
a way to ask it properly. That is the incredible&nbsp;
world we live in today. What a time to be alive!

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:47.220
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

